## Research question

Investigate changes in dust availability and provenance across the observed glacial and interglacial intervals in the supplied Greenland ice-core record. Estimate the timing and magnitude of changes using concentration and particle-size observations, and examine whether regional isotope measurements support the same interpretation. Assess what the combined evidence establishes about changes in the surrounding ice-margin environment. Choose and justify your analytical approach. Submit a scientific report, executable code, machine-readable results and informative figures. Quantify uncertainty, examine robustness to consequential analytical choices, and distinguish conclusions supported by the observations from assumptions and unresolved alternatives.

